BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Anila Quayyum Agha: All the Flowers Are for Me
DTSTART:20250514T000000
DTEND:20250514T020000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:5a4a74d21193306bfe83ef49f2a7f6@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Persian and Turkish architecture\, textiles and miniature pain
 tings inspire the precise\, stylized floral forms that compose Anila Quayy
 um Agha’s sculptural chamber of light and shadow. This luminous installa
 tion located in the Wheatland Family gallery provides an opportunity to co
 ntemplate the differences and commonalities that shape our lives and relat
 ionships. Originally from Lahore\, Pakistan\, and now living in the US\, A
 gha is acutely attuned to the social codes that inform the lives of Muslim
  women and all immigrants. She describes this work as her effort to create
  a sense of how women can reclaim and safely open up private space to welc
 ome others. Located in the Wheatland Family Gallery. Share your impression
 s with us on social media using #AlltheFlowersAreforMe.\n\nSources: Meet B
 oston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/anila-quayyum-agha%3a-
 all-the-flowers-are-for-me/85579/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, 161 Essex Street\, Salem\, MA\, 01970-3783
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/anila-quayyum-agha%3a-all-the-flowers
 -are-for-me/85579/
END:VEVENT
