BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Music America
DTSTART:20260625T000000
DTEND:20260625T020000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:248a936e9d33fa609d278e948de737@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Check out artifacts from The Beatles\, Prince\, Elvis Presley
 \, Madonna\, Jimi Hendrix & more! Music runs through the veins of America.
  Since the nation’s inception two and a half centuries ago\, music has i
 nformed our national identity\, interpreted it\, and inspired it. Whether 
 sacred or secular\, urban or rural\, folk or pop\, classical or experiment
 al\, it all adds up to the soundtrack of our American story. MUSIC AMERICA
  tells the complex story of American music through instruments\, hand-writ
 ten lyrics\, books\, photographs\, costumes\, and other objects from major
  artists across genres and generations. Featuring more than 100 legendary 
 artifacts from artists ranging from Public Enemy to Elvis Presley\, the ex
 hibit showcases stage outfits worn by Aerosmith’s Joe Perry\, Boston’s
  Tom Scholz\, and Elvis\, Chuck D’s handwritten “Fight the Power” ly
 rics\, and items from Bo Diddley\, Ella Fitzgerald\, Kurt Cobain\, Michael
  Jackson\, Bruce Springsteen and more. This exhibit is curated by and pres
 ented in partnership with the Bruce Springsteen Archives & Center for Amer
 ican Music. The Bruce Springsteen Archives & Center for American Music pre
 serves the legacy of Bruce Springsteen and celebrates the history of Ameri
 can music and its diversity of artists and genres. Our mission is two-fold
 . The Springsteen Archives serves as the official repository for materials
  related to Springsteen and the E Street Band\, including photographs\, hi
 storic memorabilia\, oral histories\, and more. The Center for American Mu
 sic explores American music more broadly. We accomplish this by producing 
 exhibitions\, concerts\, and educational programming that explores and hon
 ors the cultural impact of American music past\, present\, and future. For
  further information\, please visit www.springsteenarchives.org.\n\nSource
 s: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/music-america
 /88811/
LOCATION:Boch Center Wang Theatre\, 270 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA\, 021
 16
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/music-america/88811/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tour of Harvard
DTSTART:20260626T000000
DTEND:20261231T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:7c5572955a5d617c0b6f764ed5d8da@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Trademark Tours for their flagship Hahvahd Tour and learn
  about 4 centuries of Harvard history\, including stories about the 7 pres
 idents who went to Harvard. The Hahvahd Tour: Harvard student guides greet
  you right in Harvard Square. The tour is scripted to be an entertaining\,
  theatrical experience - you'll have fun learning about Harvard! Our tours
  are led in English. For those who do not speak English we also provide co
 mplimentary written translations in French\, Spanish\, German\, Italian\, 
 Simplified Chinese\, Korean\, and Portuguese which allow guests to read al
 ong during the tour. Harvard Main Tour Stops Include: Harvard Yard - inclu
 ding Old Yard and New Yard Historic Buildings - Memorial Hall\, Sever Hall
 \, The Widener Library and the Harvard Lampoon The famous John Harvard Sta
 tue Surrounding Neighborhood of Harvard Square - including the Plaza\, Win
 throp Park and Mt. Auburn Street Tour Themes Include: Harvard History - in
 cluding the untold stories and lore of Harvard University Harvard Culture 
 - stories and tips from current students about what it's like to live and 
 study at Harvard Famous Harvardians - learn about the most famous people t
 o attend Harvard Harvard Tour Guides: Tour guides are current Harvard unde
 rgraduate students\, graduate students and Harvard alumni.\n\nSources: Mee
 t Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/tour-of-harvard/398
 15/
LOCATION:Trademark Tours - Tours of Harvard and MIT\, Harvard Square 1380 
 Massachusetts Ave\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/tour-of-harvard/39815/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tour of MIT
DTSTART:20260626T000000
DTEND:20261231T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:42a9c84f43cc838a35554990d002a5@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Trademark Tours for our MIT Tour and learn about the hist
 ory\, innovation\, culture\, and student life of one of the world’s most
  influential universities. The MIT Tour MIT student guides greet you on ca
 mpus and lead you through an engaging\, informative\, and entertaining exp
 erience. Along the way\, guests explore some of MIT’s most recognizable 
 spaces\, including Killian Court\, the Great Dome\, the Stata Center\, the
  MIT Media Lab\, the Green Building\, and the Infinite Corridor. The tour 
 highlights MIT’s role in science\, technology\, engineering\, entreprene
 urship\, and global innovation\, while also giving guests a look at everyd
 ay student life on campus. Our tours are led in English. For guests who do
  not speak English\, we also provide complimentary written translations in
  Spanish and Simplified Chinese\, allowing guests to read along during the
  tour. Tour themes include MIT history\, campus culture\, student traditio
 ns\, famous MIT figures\, groundbreaking research\, and stories from curre
 nt students about what it is like to live\, study\, and build at MIT. MIT 
 Tour Guides Tour guides are current MIT undergraduate students\, graduate 
 students\, and MIT alumni.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://ww
 w.meetboston.com/event/tour-of-mit/91252/
LOCATION:Trademark Tours - Tours of Harvard and MIT\, Trademark Tours 67 M
 t. Auburn Street\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/tour-of-mit/91252/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chinatown Food & Culture Tour: Dumplings to Dim Sum
DTSTART:20260709T000000
DTEND:20260709T020000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:195752b84edfe9904c9af7730c8c4a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Dumplings to Dim Sum takes you beyond the gateway and into the
  heart of one of Boston's most vibrant neighborhoods. Discover the rich hi
 story\, culture\, and incredible flavors of Chinatown as you visit beloved
  family-run restaurants and hidden local gems. Savor generous tastings of 
 handmade dumplings\, flaky pastries\, and authentic regional Chinese speci
 alties while learning how generations of immigrants built and preserved th
 is thriving community. Along the way\, your local guide shares stories of 
 resilience\, tradition\, and the people behind the neighborhood's most bel
 oved eateries. Enjoy small groups (maximum 12 guests)\, a relaxed walking 
 pace\, and plenty of insider recommendations to help you continue explorin
 g Chinatown long after the tour ends. Come hungry—you'll leave with a de
 eper appreciation for Boston's Chinatown and the unforgettable flavors tha
 t make it one of the city's best-kept culinary treasures. MORE INFO/ BUY T
 ICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/eve
 nt/chinatown-food-%26-culture-tour%3a-dumplings-to-dim-sum/91660/
