SUMMARY:Murder Mystery Co. Dinner Theater Show
DTSTART:20260710T000000
DTEND:20261218T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:798e18f3cfc48bc034ca68383997cf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the murder mystery experience that puts YOU in the spotli
 ght in Boston’s Gaming District. This comedic dinner theater show at Exc
 hange Street Bistro is the killer game everyone’s dying to play. Don’t
  let this unforgettable event pass you by! At this event like no other\, y
 ou’ll play along as a detective or play a part as a suspect in the crime
 . Work with other guests to crack the case over a mouthwatering three-cour
 se meal\, and discover whodunnit before the killer gets away! Mingle and c
 onnect with other teams and intriguing suspects\, discover clues\, uncover
  shocking secrets\, and unleash your inner child’s imagination during th
 is interactive comedic experience. But watch out! The killer could be anyo
 ne… even YOU! Participate in a new mystery every month! From the glitz o
 f 1930s Hollywood in “Best Laid Plans” to the roaring 1920s with “De
 ath of a Gangster\,” each event offers unforgettable thrills. Boogie at 
 a 1950s sock hop\, solve a 90s crime in “Good Riddance\,” or celebrate
  the season with “The Most Wonderful Crime of the Year.” Whether it's 
 a billionaire’s masquerade\, a 1980s bash\, or a chilling wedding-themed
  whodunit\, there’s a unique mystery waiting for you. Mark your calendar
  and join the fun at Exchange Street Bistro in Boston! LEARN MORE / GET TI
 CKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/even
 t/murder-mystery-co-dinner-theater-show/90359/
LOCATION:Exchange Street Bistro\, Malden\, Exchange Street Bistro 67 Excha
 nge Street\, Malden\, MA\, 02148
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/murder-mystery-co-dinner-theater-show
 /90359/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pop Quiz: 1776
DTSTART:20260710T000000
DTEND:20270630T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:88d223661f590833818890543259aa@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step back into the 18th century and put your detective skills 
 to the test! Pop Quiz: 1776 takes you on a four-museum adventure to uncove
 r surprising ways that life at Harvard was both similar to and—or differ
 ent from —today. Would Harvard students in 1776 have known about the thi
 ngs we see and do today? Take a guess\, then search for specific objects a
 cross our four museums—the Harvard Museum of Natural History\, the Peabo
 dy Museum of Archaeology & Ethnology\, the Harvard Museum of the Ancient N
 ear East\, and the Collection of Historical Scientific Instruments—to ch
 eck your answers. Pro tip: join us any Sunday–Friday 11:00 am–4:00 pm 
 to access all four museums! Check museum's website for closure dates. LEAR
 N MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meet
 boston.com/event/pop-quiz%3a-1776/91664/
LOCATION:Harvard Museum of Natural History\, 26 Oxford Street\, Cambridge
 \, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/pop-quiz%3a-1776/91664/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Taste of the Freedom Trail Downtown Boston Food Tour
DTSTART:20260710T000000
DTEND:20260710T020000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:e0ae51693e47ed4a7e3bfbccf78343@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A Taste of the Freedom Trail combines Boston's most iconic lan
 dmarks with the city's legendary local foods. Walk the historic Freedom Tr
 ail while enjoying generous tastings of New England favorites like creamy 
 clam chowder\, buttery lobster rolls\, and other local specialties at belo
 ved restaurants along the way. More than a history tour or a food tour\, t
 his is Boston's story told through its flavors. Along the route\, your loc
 al guide shares fascinating stories of Indigenous foodways\, colonial trad
 itions\, immigration\, and the people who shaped the city's culinary ident
 ity. Enjoy seated tastings at several restaurants\, small groups (maximum 
 12 guests)\, water provided throughout the tour\, and plenty of insider re
 commendations to help you make the most of your time in Boston. Come hungr
 y—you'll leave full of great food\, local history\, and hidden gems! MOR
 E INFO/ BUY TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetb
 oston.com/event/taste-of-the-freedom-trail-downtown-boston-food-tour/91656
 /
