BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:20th Annual Holidays at Highfield ’Twas the Night Before Christm
 as: Life Above & Below Stairs
DTSTART:20261119T000000
DTEND:20261220T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:bb514c292a14649372c6caac21a5be@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:November 19 - December 20 Thursdays\, Fridays\, Saturdays\, & 
 Sundays\, 10:00AM - 4:00PM Highfield Hall & Gardens 56 Highfield Drive\, F
 almouth\, MA Celebrating 20 years of holiday magic at Highfield Hall & Gar
 dens. This year’s Holidays at Highfield exhibition\, ’Twas the Night B
 efore Christmas: Life Above & Below Stairs\, invites visitors to experienc
 e the final hours before Christmas morning in a grand Gilded Age mansion. 
 As the Beebe family eagerly awaits the holiday ‘above stairs’\, the se
 rvants ‘below stairs’ work tirelessly behind the scenes to prepare for
  the festivities ahead. Filled with festive beauty\, historic charm\, and 
 delightful discoveries\, the exhibition offers an immersive holiday experi
 ence for visitors of all ages. The beloved Gift Gallery returns with handc
 rafted artisan gifts\, while the holiday craft room provides hands-on fun 
 for children and families. Gather family and friends and celebrate the sea
 son with one of Cape Cod’s most beloved holiday traditions. $20 for Memb
 ers / $25 for Non-members\, Children & Military are FREE $35 per Adult for
  Friday Twilight Hours (libations & light snacks provided) Pre-registratio
 n is encouraged. 508-495-1878 or visit highfieldhallandgardens.org\n\nSour
 ces: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/20
 th-annual-holidays-at-highfield-%e2%80%99twas-the-night-before-christmas%3
 a-life-above-%26-below-stairs/52804/
LOCATION:Highfield Hall & Gardens\, 56 Highfield Drive\, Falmouth\, MA\, 0
 2540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/20th-annual-holidays-at-highfield
 -%e2%80%99twas-the-night-before-christmas%3a-life-above-%26-below-stairs/5
 2804/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:9 to 5: The Musical
DTSTART:20261119T190000
DTEND:20261119T210000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:a416626ed5e20bf161353d0e77cf87@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Pour Yourself a Cup of Ambition: Triton Theatre Presents 9 to 
 5: The Musical! Tumble out of bed and stumble to the box office\, because 
 Triton Regional High School Theatre is clocking in for its biggest fall mu
 sical yet! With music and lyrics by country legend Dolly Parton and a book
  by Patricia Resnick\, 9 to 5: The Musical is based on the hit 1980 film a
 nd is packed with toe-tapping songs\, big laughs\, and a whole lot of hear
 t. Meet Violet\, Judy\, and Doralee: three hard working coworkers who have
  finally had enough of their boss\, Franklin Hart Jr.\, a sexist\, egotist
 ical\, lying\, hypocritical bigot who takes credit for their work and trea
 ts them like they’re part of the furniture. When a wild chain of events 
 puts the boss in their hands\, the trio seizes the chance to turn the offi
 ce upside down. Before long\, they’re running the company better than he
  ever did. But can they keep their scheme under wraps long enough to chang
 e the workplace for good? Bursting with friendship\, comedy\, and the cour
 age to stand up for yourself\, 9 to 5 is a celebration of people who refus
 e to settle for less than they deserve. It’s a story that fits right in 
 with our mission at THS Theatre: welcoming everyone into our theatrical fa
 mily and captivating audiences with performances that make them laugh\, th
 ink\, and cheer. Audience Advisory: Recommended for Ages 12 and Up 9 to 5:
  The Musical is set in a 1970s office and deals with mature themes. The sh
 ow includes workplace sexual harassment\, innuendo and suggestive humor\, 
 some strong language\, a scene depicting drug use\, and comedic violence. 
 We recommend this production for audiences ages 12 and up. Parents and gua
 rdians are encouraged to use their own judgment for younger viewers. Quest
 ions? Contact us at tritonarts@gmail.com.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEve
 nt page: https://northofboston.org/event/9-to-5-the-musical/
LOCATION:Triton Regional High School Auditorium\, 112 Elm Street\, Byfield
 \, MA\, 01922
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/9-to-5-the-musical/
END:VEVENT
