BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Life of George B. Schaller and the Future of Conservation
DTSTART:20261119T000000
DTEND:20261119T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:7dae3fd34319cc9fbf37667520bc80@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Field biologist and conservationist George B. Schaller is reno
 wned for revolutionizing the study of wildlife by observing animals in the
 ir natural habitats. He has also been a powerful advocate for protecting w
 ilderness and animal species across the globe. Born in 1933 in Berlin to a
 n American mother and a German father in Berlin\, Schaller spent his war
 ‑torn childhood searching for peace among wild creatures. His efforts to
 ok him around the world to study Congo mountain gorillas\, Himalayan snow 
 leopards\, Brazilian jaguars\, Tibetan brown bears\, and many others. Befo
 re Jane Goodall or Dian Fossey\, Schaller revealed the rich emotional and 
 social lives of these primates and predators. Drawing from her new book Ho
 mesick for a World Unknown: The Life of George B. Schaller (Penguin Press
 \, 2026)\, Miriam Horn will trace his remarkable career. She will highligh
 t his views on conservation and the path to survival he mapped for us all
 —challenging us to rethink our place in the natural world. Copies of Hom
 esick for a World Unknown will be available for purchase after the program
 . Free event parking is available with registration. Register by November 
 18 to receive parking registration instructions. Advance registration is r
 ecommended to attend in-person or online. Presented by the Peabody Museum 
 of Archaeology & Ethnology\, the Harvard Museum of Natural History\, and t
 he Harvard Museums of Science & Culture. Speaker: Miriam Horn\, Author LEA
 RN MORE HERE\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.c
 om/event/the-life-of-george-b-schaller-and-the-future-of-conservation/9420
 5/
LOCATION:Harvard Museums of Science & Culture\, 24 Oxford Street\, Geologi
 cal Lecture Hall\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/the-life-of-george-b-schaller-and-the
 -future-of-conservation/94205/
END:VEVENT
