DESCRIPTION:Joanne Chang\, James Beard Award-winning chef\, restaurateur\,
  and author\; Adrian Miller\, two-time James Beard Award-winning culinary 
 author\; and James Beard Award-winning Mashpee Wampanoag Chef Sherry Pockn
 ett discuss immigrant and Indigenous contributions to American food tradit
 ions. Writer\, stylist\, and former food editor of The Boston Globe Sheryl
  Julian moderates. Interested in-person Forum attendees may pre-order copi
 es of The Joy of Cookies by Joanne Chang\; The President's Kitchen Cabinet
  by Adrian Miller\; and Asian Heritage Chefs in White House History: Cooki
 ng to the President's Taste by Adrian Miller and Deborah Chang for pickup 
 at the JFK Presidential Library & Museum for the Forum on November 19\, 20
 26. For those attending the program\, authors will be signing copies of th
 e book. This item is not eligible for shipping as it is available exclusiv
 ely for on-site Forum attendees. LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent
  page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/your-house-and-the-white-house/941
 73/
