BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Public Reception: Assets for Artists 2026 Showcase
DTSTART:20261120T000000
DTEND:20261120T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:49ad2bda366b677ac05d61f133c820@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Assets for Artists’ (A4A) Capacity-Building Program provides
  individualized\, artist-centered professional development to help artists
  strengthen their creative practice\, pursue values-driven careers\, build
  mutually-supportive networks and find resources to achieve long term sust
 ainability and self-determination. Over the course of six months\, this co
 hort of Capacity-Building artists attended a series of gatherings and work
 shops aimed at simultaneously building professional skills and creative co
 mmunity. Now\, artists proudly showcase their work as part of this group e
 xhibition at ArtsWorcester. The showcase features the work of dancers\, ch
 oreographers\, poets\, playwrights\, mixed media visual artists\, and more
 . Friday\, November 20\, 6 - 8 PM ArtsWorcester // 44 Portland Street\, Wo
 rcester\, MA Third-floor Davis Art Gallery with stairs and elevator access
 ible Free and open to the public // Cash bar Exhibiting artists include: A
 shley MacLure\, mixed media Cynthia B. Sellers\, mixed media Ellen Oliver
 \, interdisciplinary choreographer Jasmin Rivas\, writer Jill Strait\, vis
 ual artist and musician Kay Lee\, visual artist Mandy Gutmann-Gonzalez\, w
 riter Mari Saxon\, photographer Nick Baker\, theater artist Susana Rodrigu
 ez\, dancer and choreographer The A4A Worcester County Capacity-Building p
 rogram and culminating showcase comes with the support of Greater Worceste
 r Community Foundation\, the region's largest funder of arts programs and 
 a member of the Creative Commonwealth Initiative. The Assets for Artists 2
 026 Showcase will be on view at ArtsWorcester from November 12 to December
  13\, 2026 during gallery hours: WED - SUN\, 12pm - 5pm. On Thursday\, Dec
 ember 10\, ArtsWorcester will be open until 7 PM for late night hours. Gal
 lery hours are always open and free to all. // Images courtesy of exhibiti
 ng Assets for Artists Worcester Capacity-Building cohort members: Mari Sax
 on\, Cynthia B. Sellers\, Jasmin Rivas\, and Susana Rodriguez.\n\nSources:
  Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma
 .org/event/public-reception%3a-assets-for-artists-2026-showcase/31268/
LOCATION:ArtsWorcester\, 44 Portland St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/public-reception%3a-assets-for
 -artists-2026-showcase/31268/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sara Landry
DTSTART:20261120T000000
DTEND:20261120T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:c26920e0f4c26d63921bb61205d3e5@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Sara Landry is a DJ\, producer and record label head who trans
 forms hard dance into high-pressure\, transcendent experiences through her
  driving\, divinely feminine lens. More than just an artist\, Landry is a 
 cultural architect operating at the edges of hard dance. Her work is built
  on physical\, emotional and sonic pressure\, resulting in a sound that fa
 vors intensity and demands attention. As one of the most in-demand names i
 n music\, her boundary-breaking vision has transformed the scene\, pushing
  hard dance beyond genre into an authored vision. Landry’s productions a
 re not designed to decorate a room\, rather\, to transform it with structu
 red intention\, rupture and momentum. After emerging from the underground 
 with her viral breakout 2023 Boiler Room set – which remains one of the 
 highest streamed Boiler Room of the past two years with over 10 million vi
 ews – the multi-hyphenate has amassed a devoted\, cult-like following as
  she continues to defy convention with her unadulterated ferocity and indi
 sputable originality. Taking her artistry to unprecedented levels\, Landry
 ’s live concepts – ETERNALISM\, her high-octane physical manifestation
  of communion and catharsis\; and BLOOD OATH\, her trailblazing set concep
 t\, carefully curated as a testament to her affinity for the unconventiona
 l and her uncompromised commitment to fostering the often overlooked femal
 e community in electronic music – offer audiences one-of-a-kind experien
 ces as she transforms performance into a collective act\, entwining sound 
 with ritual\, restraint and release. Her sets are fully immersive rituals
 \, built to be shared\, endured and remembered. With a commanding presence
  and a raw power that’s impossible to ignore\, Landry has solidified her
 self as a mainstay on some of the world’s most influential stages includ
 ing Coachella\, Tomorrowland\, EDC Las Vegas\, Creamfields and more. Beyon
 d her own output\, the multi-hyphenate remains fiercely committed to creat
 ing spaces for artists she believes in through her label\, HEKATE\, where 
 she pushes past the confines of traditional power structures and uplifts a
 rtists in the category.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.m
 eetboston.com/event/sara-landry/93205/
LOCATION:Roadrunner\, 89 Guest Street Boston Landing\, Brighton\, MA\, 021
 35
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/sara-landry/93205/
END:VEVENT
