SUMMARY:Retired Detective Lieutenant Brian O'Hara will discuss his new tru
 e crime book "The Rest of the Story"
DTSTART:20261121T000000
DTEND:20261121T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:244f89db213c25c15e58d706c45848@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Retired Detective Lieutenant Brian O'Hara will discuss his new
  true crime book "The Rest of the Story" as well as sign personalized copi
 es at the MSPMLC. This book explores real-life forensic cases from the Mas
 sachusetts State Police\, each highlighting a different forensic disciplin
 e utilized to collect and analyze evidence left at crime scenes. Over his 
 forty-five-year career in forensics\, DLT O'Hara documented crime scenes t
 hrough photography\, video\, and written reports\, collecting crucial evid
 ence\, and conducted scientific forensic analyses of fingerprints\, footwe
 ar impressions\, tire tracks\, and blood evidence. He has testified as an 
 expert witness in Massachusetts Superior Courts\, presenting my findings t
 o help bring justice to the victims and their families.\n\nSources: Discov
 er Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/ev
 ent/retired-detective-lieutenant-brian-ohara-will-discuss-his-new-true-cri
 me-book-the-rest-of-the-story/31415/
