SUMMARY:Seasonal Saturday Tours!
DTSTART:20261121T110000
DTEND:20261121T160000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:7ecc55cf01179eaf641acbba7f6556@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Fall and Winter Guided Tours at the Museum of Old Newbury Begi
 nning in mid-October\, 2026\, the Museum of Old Newbury will open its door
 s for guided tours every Saturday. Tours begin on the hour from 11:00 a.m.
  to 4:00 p.m. (last tour departs at 3:00 p.m.). Please note: certain dates
  are excluded\, and tours are weather permitting. Step back in time as you
 r knowledgeable guide leads you through two floors of our 1808 brick Feder
 al-style home\, where every room is filled with objects\, stories\, and me
 mories of Old Newbury. Along the way\, you’ll hear tales of the families
  who lived here\, discover treasures from our collection\, and gain new in
 sight into the rich history of Newburyport and the surrounding area. Wheth
 er you’re a first-time visitor or a longtime resident\, this is your cha
 nce to experience the museum in a whole new way—through a carefully cura
 ted\, guided experience designed to bring history to life.\n\nSources: Nor
 th of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/seasonal-saturda
 y-tours-2/2026-11-21/
LOCATION:Museum of Old Newbury\, 98 High Street\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/seasonal-saturday-tours-2/2026-11-21/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sound by Sound with J.D. Scrimgeour and Aidan Scrimgeour
DTSTART:20261121T190000
DTEND:20261121T203000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:3c8ab0dc754aea3259f46c4bee64f9@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Sound by Sound is a father-and-son collaboration blending musi
 c and poetry. The event features Aidan Scrimgeour and his father\, J.D.\, 
 Salem’s inaugural poet laureate and longtime Salem State Professor\, per
 forming poems by J.D. alongside music composed by Aidan and improvised col
 lectively by participating musicians. The pair collaborated previously on 
 the musical\, Only Human\, which premiered in Salem in 2014. Aidan Scrimge
 our is a multi-instrumentalist\, composer and teacher. Based in Brooklyn\,
  NY since 2019\, he is active in various folk\, jazz and improvised music 
 scenes\, performing on piano\, organ and accordion. He is the co-founder o
 f the Brooklyn Porch Music Multigenerational Big Band and works as a music
  teaching artist with the National Dance Institute in the NYC public schoo
 ls. J.D. Scrimgeour is the author of six books of poetry and three of nonf
 iction. He also is the editor of Pieces of Salem: An Anthology of Salem Vo
 ices\, a collection of writing about Salem by over 130 of its citizens to 
 help commemorate the city’s 400th anniversary. This event is J.D.’s fi
 nal performance in his role as Poet Laureate. The Salem State Recital Hall
  is located on the ground floor of 71 Loring Avenue.\n\nSources: North of 
 Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/sound-by-sound-with-j-
 d-scrimgeour-and-aidan-scrimgeour/
LOCATION:Salem State University Recital Hall\, Classroom Building\, Centra
 l Campus\, 71 Loring Avenue\, Salem\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/sound-by-sound-with-j-d-scrimgeour-and
 -aidan-scrimgeour/
END:VEVENT
