BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samantha Fish
DTSTART:20261122T000000
DTEND:20261122T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:8f276e6abf44183a7d75977efd3c24@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Samantha Fish is a two-time GRAMMY-nominated guitarist\, singe
 r\, and songwriter widely recognized as one of the leading artists in cont
 emporary blues and roots music. A Kansas Music Hall of Fame inductee and m
 ultiple Blues Music Awards winner\, she is celebrated for her electrifying
  guitar playing\, powerhouse vocals\, and emotionally charged songwriting.
  Through relentless touring and a string of critically acclaimed releases
 \, Fish has built an international audience\, with all nine of her albums 
 landing on the Billboard Blues Albums chart. A commanding live performer\,
  she has toured extensively around the world\, appeared at the New Orleans
  Jazz & Heritage Festival\, shared stages with artists including Slash and
  The Rolling Stones\, and performed at Crossroads Guitar Festival. Whether
  on record or onstage\, Fish continues to expand the reach of modern blues
  while forging a powerful connection with audiences worldwide. LEARN MORE 
 / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.
 com/event/samantha-fish/92098/
LOCATION:The Wilbur\, 246 Tremont Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/samantha-fish/92098/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Schubert / Bruckner
DTSTART:20261122T000000
DTEND:20261122T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:004c79ef1558f0c4f523c6cec4f16b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The Boston Philharmonic Orchestra (BPO) continues its 48th and
  final celebratory season on Sunday\, November 22\, 2026 at 3:00 p.m.\, ex
 ploring the Austrian symphonic tradition with works by Schubert and Bruckn
 er\, led by conductor Benjamin Zander at Symphony Hall. The BPO concert is
  paired with Benjamin Zander’s popular Guide to the Music pre-concert ta
 lk beginning at 1:45 p.m.\, engaging classical music novices and aficionad
 os alike in the concert experience. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS\n\nSources: M
