BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between Season's: Off Season Tours at the Museums on the Green
DTSTART:20261128T000000
DTEND:20261128T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:4e56d5d361a1c8dc3d79eeb5da4b80@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Between Seasons: Off-Season Tours at the Museums on the Green 
 Discover Falmouth’s historic homes and gardens in the calm of the off-se
 ason. Step into Falmouth’s historic homes during the quieter months with
  Between the Seasons\, our off-season tour series at the Museums on the Gr
 een. Enjoy an intimate\, guided exploration of the Wicks House\, Conant Ho
 use\, and Cultural Center American Revolution exhibition in a peaceful set
 ting\, hear the stories of the families who lived here\, and enjoy a more 
 intimate look at our preserved space beyond the summer crowds. It’s the 
 perfect way to discover local history at a slower\, reflective pace. Free 
 Admission. Come anytime during our open hours. Self-guided exhibit touring
  in 2 houses\, and docent-led tours of our 1790 Dr. Wicks House. You will 
 find our tour guides & volunteers in the Hallet Barn Visitor’s Center & 
 Whaling Wives Gift Shop. Kids Activities: -Village Green Scavenger Hunt bo
 oklet -Activity Backpack full of games -Wicks House scavenger hunt Visit u
 s from 10am-2pm on the following dates: November 28th\, 2026 December 5th
 \, 2026 – Wreath Sale & Holiday Market day!\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber
 \nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/between-seasons%3a-off-
 season-tours-at-the-museums-on-the-green/52637/
LOCATION:Falmouth Museums on the Green\, 55 & 65 Palmer Avenue\, Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/between-seasons%3a-off-season-tou
 rs-at-the-museums-on-the-green/52637/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beverly’s Inaugural Holiday Pops Concert
DTSTART:20261128T180000
DTEND:20261128T220000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:84194cdb4a61cc08efd93c1d5b4bd4@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A true Boston-quality holiday concert—right at home in Bever
 ly. Experience the magic of a full 35-piece professional orchestra\, led b
 y internationally renowned conductor Dr. Dirk Hillyer. ​Celebrate the se
 ason with a spectacular evening of live orchestral music at the historic L
 arcom Theatre. The Dirk Hillyer Festival Orchestra brings the excitement a
 nd musicianship of a big-city Holiday Pops concert to the North Shore for 
 Beverly’s inaugural Holiday Pops celebration. This high-energy\, heartwa
 rming holiday performance is fun for the whole family\, featuring beloved 
 seasonal favorites\, audience sing-alongs\, and show-stopping performances
  by professional soloists. Expect a few surprises along the way—includin
 g a special visit from Santa himself! It’s the perfect way to kick off t
 he holiday season with friends\, family\, and community. Classic holiday c
 heer\, Broadway-level musicianship\, and a historic hometown theatre.​ A
 ge Recommendation: All ages Proud to welcome soloists Nathan Seavey and Be
 thany Vahn to accompany the orchestra for several holiday favorites. Date:
  Sat.\, November 28\, 2026 Time: 7:00 PM\; Doors & Bar 6:00 PM Duration: A
 pprox. two hours with intermission Tickets: $30–$50 (not including fees)
  Venue: Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis St.\, Beverly\, MA\n\nSources: North of
  Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/beverlys-inaugural-ho
 liday-pops-concert-2/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/beverlys-inaugural-holiday-pops-concer
 t-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bim Skala Bim w/ special guest The Chip Rockers
DTSTART:20261128T200000
DTEND:20261128T230000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:58291b3c4ab2a592fae0ba2a00a51b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Bim Skala Bim formed in Boston\, MA over 40 years ago as a Ska
  Rocksteady and Reggae band that was influenced by the bands in England’
 s 2 Tone movement\, as well as the music of the Clash\, UB40 and Bob Marle
 y. Bim’s infectious Boston Blue Beat sound led them to be one of the pre
 mier bands kick-starting the Third Wave of Ska in the 1980s. Other bands q
 uickly followed their example resulting in a lively scene in Boston and mu
 ch of the United States.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://
 northofboston.org/event/bim-skala-bim-w-special-guest-the-chip-rockers/
