BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeowner Resources - Renovating your Historic Home
DTSTART:20261128T000000
DTEND:20261128T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:745c4f9cacbd440de786d85041e3f8@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Falmouth’s Historic Homes: Stories\, Preservation & Practica
 l Advice New Date! November 28th | 2:15 PM Whether you own an older home\,
  are thinking about renovating\, or simply enjoy learning about Falmouth
 ’s history\, join us for an informative and engaging afternoon exploring
  the joys and challenges of caring for historic properties. Our Robert G. 
 Ripley Jr. Fellowship student\, Lainey Bechta\, will share stories about s
 everal historic houses in Falmouth who now have date plaques\, along with 
 practical information about renovating older homes and understanding mater
 ials such as lead and other potentially hazardous substances that were onc
 e commonly used in home construction. We’ll also discuss our newly launc
 hed Historic Date Plaque Program\, which offers homeowners an opportunity 
 to discover and celebrate the history of their own properties. Learn how t
 o apply for a custom exterior plaque commemorating your home’s original 
 construction date\, along with a researched historical report documenting 
 its history and previous owners. Part of our Fix the Wicks community educa
 tion initiative\, this program reflects our commitment to helping preserve
  Falmouth’s architectural heritage and connecting residents with the his
 tory of the places they call home. Free and open to the public. Donations 
 gratefully accepted. Register Here\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent pag
 e: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/homeowner-resources-renovating-you
 r-historic-home/52798/
LOCATION:Falmouth Museums on the Green\, 55 & 65 Palmer Avenue\, Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/homeowner-resources-renovating-yo
 ur-historic-home/52798/
END:VEVENT
