BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly International Book Club - Ali and Nino
DTSTART:20261202T000000
DTEND:20261202T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:48b9e739894661634a806de89e2831@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:International Book Group – Ali & Nino: A Love Story by Kurba
 n Said The International Book Group at West Falmouth Library is a voluntee
 r-led group that meets on the first Wednesday of each month 3:45-5 p.m. Se
 lections have either foreign settings or foreign authors\, usually both. N
 ew members are always welcome! Annual registration is requested to receive
  important communications about schedule or location changes\; register be
 low. Meetings are both in-person and on Zoom. The Wednesday\, December 2 m
 eeting will discuss Ali & Nino: A Love Story by Kurban Said. From the auth
 or of The Girl from the Golden Horn\, a novel of the enduring love between
  childhood friends divided by war & their separate cultures. First publish
 ed in Vienna in 1937\, this classic story of romance and adventure has bee
 n compared to Dr. Zhivago and Romeo and Juliet. Ali and Nino is Kurban Sai
 d’s masterpiece. It is a captivating novel as evocative of the exotic de
 sert landscape as it is of the passion between two people pulled apart by 
 culture\, religion\, and war. “One feels as if one had dug up buried tre
 asure…one feels completely caught up in the novel’s exotic setting…a
 n epic of cultural change that seems more immediate than this morning’s 
 headlines.” —The New York Times “Poignant and beautiful…alive with
  a vividly unique vision of colliding culture and enduring love.” —New
 sweek Register Here\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.
 capecodchamber.org/event/monthly-international-book-club-ali-and-nino/5227
 4/
LOCATION:West Falmouth Library\, 575 West Falmouth Highway\, West Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02574
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/monthly-international-book-club-a
 li-and-nino/52274/
END:VEVENT
