BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261205T111500
DTEND:20261205T161500
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:25843786d0ce5d39d8b6ecb21c4d4f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-12-05/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 2-05/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:15th Annual Ukulele Festival
DTSTART:20261206T000000
DTEND:20261206T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:bc7a87985aed183a93886bd28c6daa@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to strum\, sing\, and smile! Cotuit Center for the A
 rts is thrilled to present our 15th Annual Ukulele Festival\, a joyful\, h
 oliday-themed celebration of one of the world’s friendliest instruments.
  This beloved annual tradition features some of the Cape’s most talented
  ukulele players\, performing an eclectic mix of holiday favorites\, pop h
 its\, and feel-good classics. The evening will conclude with the much-love
 d “Uke-A-Long” finale\, inviting everyone with a ukulele to join the p
 erformers on stage for a rousing group performance you won’t forget. The
  festival is once again organized by Steve Gregory\, owner of Score Music 
 in Sandwich and longtime ukulele teacher at Cotuit Center for the Arts. A 
 passionate advocate for the instrument\, Steve loves how the uke brings pe
 ople together: “It’s a nice\, friendly\, affordable folk instrument th
 at is easy and comfortable to play\,” he says. “It appeals to all ages
 —I’ve had students as young as 4 and into their 80s. Being on stage wi
 th 45 or 50 people all playing and singing together is an intense\, profou
 nd experience.” Whether you’re a seasoned strummer\, a beginner\, or s
 imply a fan of the ukulele’s cheerful charm\, the Ukulele Festival is th
 e perfect way to kick off the holiday season. Admission: $20 – FREE if y
 ou bring a ukulele and join the onstage “Uke-A-Long” finale. We would 
 like to thank Martha and Paul Ross\, whose generous support helps keep liv
 e music thriving on Cotuit’s stages.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent
  page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/15th-annual-ukulele-festival/5
 2820/
LOCATION:Cotuit Center for the Arts\, 4404 Falmouth Road\, Cotuit\, MA\, 0
 2635
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/15th-annual-ukulele-festival/5282
 0/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:47th Annual Christmas In Salem Holiday House Tour
DTSTART:20261206T113000
DTEND:20261206T160000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:3d4183278555a9c3d38bf60d4a10a1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Tickets are now available online for Historic Salem\, Inc’s 
 (HSI) annual Christmas in Salem (TM) house tour. The event takes place on 
 Saturday and Sunday\, December 5 and 6. It is the 47th year of this festiv
 e event\, where homeowners in Salem open the doors to their historic homes
  and welcome ticketholders to enjoy beautiful holiday decorations. This ye
 ar’s tour focuses on the Derby Street neighborhood. Nine historic homes 
 are open and the tour also includes stops on the campus of the House of th
 e Seven Gables plus both the Custom House and the Derby House at Salem’s
  Maritime National Historic Park. The theme for this year’s tour\, “Se
 as and Greetings” is a celebration of Salem’s rich maritime history an
 d an homage to Salem’s 400th anniversary. These private homes and histor
 ic campuses capture the history and rich architecture of the Derby Street 
 neighborhood. House tour ticketholders will enjoy a variety of seasonal en
 tertainment inside the private homes\, plus wandering carolers in the neig
 hborhood\, and activities and lectures at the area’s historic campuses a
 nd businesses. Some of these holiday delights include some tastings\, twis
 ting your own candy canes at Ye Olde Pepper Companie\, sampling sweet bite
 s at The Chocolate Pantry and at the historic Hawthorne Hotel. Other stops
  include the Real Pirates Salem\, Jolie Tea Company\, Marine Hall Mercanti
 le and Salem Wine Imports. . Tour hours are Saturday\, December 5\, 10:30 
 am – 4 pm and Sunday\, December 6\, 11:30 am – 4 pm. Tickets for Chris
 tmas in Salem are available at www.historicsalem.org at $40 for HSI member
 s\, $45 for non- members. Tickets are available for purchase at the Visito
 rs Center at The House of the Seven Gables and online the day of the tour 
 for $50.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.or
 g/event/47th-annual-christmas-in-salem-holiday-house-tour/2026-12-06/
LOCATION:House of the Seven Gables\, 115 Derby St\, Salem\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/47th-annual-christmas-in-salem-holiday
 -house-tour/2026-12-06/
END:VEVENT
