DTEND:20261210T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:eeb3e647204e22561c132297933b80@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In observation (and dubious celebration) of the 2026 EGH exhib
 it O Sordid Type: Edward Gorey’s Art of Lettering\, the House and Thache
 r Hall invite you to join us for Gorey Letters: an evening of writing the 
 alphabet in various ways. Learn the history of the typefaces Gorey drew hi
 s inspiration from and design letterforms of your very own. Tickets includ
 e refreshments and light snacks\, as well as a pen\, ink\, notepad\, and a
  pre-cut sheet of Gorey’s beloved Bristol board for your “final projec
 t.” House Members receive $10 off their tickets with the use of their co
 de at checkout. While this event is recommended for grown-ups\, the more a
 rtistically inclined young adult in your life may get something out of it 
 as well. We discourage the attendance of creatives young enough to be temp
 ted into the consumption of ink\, a pen\, or some other delectable-yet-ind
 igestible material.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.
 capecodchamber.org/event/gorey-letters%3a-a-workshop/52671/
LOCATION:Thacher Hall\, 266 Route 6A P.O. Box 237\, Yarmouth Port\, MA\, 0
 2675
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/gorey-letters%3a-a-workshop/52671
 /
