UID:707a2b5d23c7a4215f78f9db4f3bd0@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the most magical weekend of the holiday season at th
 e Cape Cod Christmas Market! https://capecodchristmasmarket.com Join us Th
 anksgiving weekend for three festive days (plus December 12) filled with h
 andcrafted gifts\, holiday shopping\, seasonal treats\, live entertainment
 \, and Christmas cheer. Whether you’re starting your holiday shopping or
  creating a new family tradition\, you’ll discover the very best of Cape
  Cod’s local makers and small businesses. Shop unique handcrafted gifts 
 from talented local artisans Support Cape Cod small businesses Find beauti
 ful holiday décor and one-of-a-kind treasures Enjoy festive food\, warm b
 everages\, and seasonal favorites Experience live holiday entertainment th
 roughout the market Visit with Santa and enjoy fun activities for the whol
 e family Help support our annual community food drive benefiting local fam
 ilies There’s nothing quite like the sights\, sounds\, and spirit of Chr
 istmas at the Cape Cod Christmas Market. Gather your family and friends an
 d enjoy a festive shopping experience filled with holiday magic. Market Da
 tes Friday\, November 27 | 11:00 AM-2:00 PM Saturday\, November 28 | 11:00
  AM-2:00 PM Sunday\, November 29 | 11:00 AM-2:00 PM Saturday\, December 12
  | 11:00 AM-2:00 PM Location Naukabout Beer Garden\, 4 Job’s Fishing Roa
 d\, Mashpee\, MA Admission is FREE! Shop local. Celebrate the season. Crea
 te lasting memories. For vendor applications\, sponsorship opportunities\,
  and additional event information\, visit CapeCodChristmasMarket.com.\n\nS
 ources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event
 /cape-cod-christmas-market/52823/
LOCATION:Lemonadio\, Mashpee\, MA
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/cape-cod-christmas-market/52823/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Christmas Around the World &#8211\; Holiday Hits 2026
DTSTART:20261212T000000
DTEND:20261212T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:ca8dd137ae36c85c7e1918c0274527@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:This December\, Cape Cod Music Society is thrilled to present 
 the 6th Annual "Christmas Around the World - Holiday Hits"\, returning big
 ger than ever with an expanded five-concert series across Cape Cod. Follow
 ing last year’s successful three-concert series\, including sold-out per
 formances\, this year’s events will bring even more opportunities to exp
 erience this extraordinary holiday tradition. Join us for an unforgettable
  evening of holiday music featuring the Cape Cod String Quartet - Dan Flon
 ta\, Jeff Pearson\, Sofia Nikas\, Nancy Torrente - and friends - Jonathan 
 Weir\, Anna McEntee\, Emma Fahle\, Antonio Abate\, William Pernice\, Bart 
 Weisman\, James Peterson and Catherine Bonnett - performing a mix of moder
 n holiday favorites and timeless classics. The program will take audiences
  on a musical sleigh ride through some of the greatest hits of the season
 \, including All I Want for Christmas\, Baby It’s Cold Outside\, Happy X
 mas (War Is Over)\, Do They Know It’s Christmas?\, Christmas (Baby Pleas
 e Come Home)\, Run Rudolph Run\, White Christmas\, Silver Bells\, The Chri
 stmas Song (Chestnuts Roasting on an Open Fire)\, Sleigh Ride\, and many m
 ore. Saturday December 12\, 2026 - 4:00 PM St. Christopher's Church - 625 
 Main St\, Chatham\, MA 02633 Tickets: https://www.capecodmusicsociety.org/
 event-details/christmas-around-the-world-holiday-hits-2026-st-christophers
 -chatham-sixth-annual-concert-series\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent p
 age: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/christmas-around-the-world-%26%2
 38211%3b-holiday-hits-2026/52749/
LOCATION:St. Christopher's Church - 625 Main St\, Chatham\, St. Christophe
 r's Church 625 Main Street\, Chatham\, MA\, 02633
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/christmas-around-the-world-%26%23
 8211%3b-holiday-hits-2026/52749/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deck the Halls at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261212T090000
DTEND:20261212T153000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:ddd55496493eb89e4311e11ef9a0de@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Holiday Season as we proudly present our 
 8th annual holiday celebration\, Deck the Halls\, a Museum-wide holiday in
 stallation! Travel back in time to a castle filled with candlelight and lu
 sh\, opulent textures inspired by the great medieval and Renaissance castl
 es of Europe. We are delighted to partner again with Elaine Quinn Interior
 s\, a boutique residential interior design firm based in Manchester-by-the
 -Sea\, to bring heightened inspiration and artistry to this year’s museu
 m-wide holiday installation. Abundant greenery and sumptuous layers of dé
 cor create a richly immersive seasonal experience throughout the Museum. W
 ander through rooms adorned with white birch and Christmas trees\, sparkli
 ng fairy lights\, hydrangea-lace garlands\, and elegant bows\, with each s
 pace transformed by its own unique holiday theme. This celebration also em
 braces the traditions of Hanukkah\, with two beautifully displayed menorah
 s adding their own warm glow to the Museum’s festive splendor. From natu
 re’s bounty of fruits and greenery to the warm glow of candlelight\, eve
 ry detail creates a feast for the senses. Along the way\, encounter a roya
 l guard of nutcrackers\, a gingerbread house replica of the Museum\, and p
 layful elves and gnomes up to mischief\, adding a touch of whimsy for litt
 le ones. In addition to the holiday installation\, guests can enjoy the te
 mporary exhibition\, “Brave-Too-Much”: The Legend of John Coffee Hays.
  Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to fully experience the h
 oliday installation and exhibition Extended Tuesday and Thursday Tour Hour
 s: New this year\, visitors can enjoy extended hours on Tuesdays and Thurs
 days\, with last entry at 7:15 p.m. These extended guided and self-guided 
 tour hours offer greater opportunities to experience the Museum after dark
 \, when holiday décor glows with flickering candlelight and twinkling lig
 hts. Upon arrival\, visitors will discover the path and outdoor Courtyard
 \, arches and towers aglow with festive holiday lighting\, creating a trul
 y magical seasonal atmosphere. Visitors will have more time to explore the
  Museum’s holiday decorations and experience the beauty of this historic
  site after dark. Admission pricing varies\, please visit our website for 
 accurate pricing. Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to take 
 in the full holiday grandeur. Museum member benefits apply.\n\nSources: No
 rth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-
 at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-12-12/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-at-hammond-castle-museu
 m/2026-12-12/
END:VEVENT
