BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Comedian PJ Thibodeau at The Sea Crest Beach Resort
DTSTART:20261219T000000
DTEND:20261219T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:365856b81887ac938800ffa6916351@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:PJ Thibodeau is a longtime favorite of the New England comedy 
 scene\, known for his road-tested storytelling\, sharp punchlines\, and hi
 larious observations on everyday life. A seasoned performer who has entert
 ained audiences throughout Boston\, Rhode Island\, Maine\, and beyond\, PJ
  brings an easygoing\, relatable style that keeps crowds laughing from beg
 inning to end. Joining him is feature comedian Dan Boulger\, who began per
 forming nationally after winning the Boston Comedy Festival in 2006 at jus
 t 20 years old and has since appeared on Comedy Central\, The Late Late Sh
 ow with Craig Ferguson\, and at the HBO Aspen Comedy Festival. Rising Bost
 on comedian Nic Sugiarto will host the evening and keep the energy high al
 l night long. Grab your tickets early for a night packed with standout New
  England comedy. Doors open at 7pm & the show starts at 8 pm. To buy ticke
 ts\, click the button below\, or call 508-274-2190 for further details. BU
 Y TICKETS\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodcha
 mber.org/event/comedian-pj-thibodeau-at-the-sea-crest-beach-resort/52521/
LOCATION:Sea Crest Beach Resort\, 350 Quaker Rd\, North Falmouth\, MA\, 02
 556
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/comedian-pj-thibodeau-at-the-sea-
 crest-beach-resort/52521/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deck the Halls at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261219T090000
DTEND:20261219T153000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:34a413a2efdda2ca14fe06c1b47e9f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Holiday Season as we proudly present our 
 8th annual holiday celebration\, Deck the Halls\, a Museum-wide holiday in
 stallation! Travel back in time to a castle filled with candlelight and lu
 sh\, opulent textures inspired by the great medieval and Renaissance castl
 es of Europe. We are delighted to partner again with Elaine Quinn Interior
 s\, a boutique residential interior design firm based in Manchester-by-the
 -Sea\, to bring heightened inspiration and artistry to this year’s museu
 m-wide holiday installation. Abundant greenery and sumptuous layers of dé
 cor create a richly immersive seasonal experience throughout the Museum. W
 ander through rooms adorned with white birch and Christmas trees\, sparkli
 ng fairy lights\, hydrangea-lace garlands\, and elegant bows\, with each s
 pace transformed by its own unique holiday theme. This celebration also em
 braces the traditions of Hanukkah\, with two beautifully displayed menorah
 s adding their own warm glow to the Museum’s festive splendor. From natu
 re’s bounty of fruits and greenery to the warm glow of candlelight\, eve
 ry detail creates a feast for the senses. Along the way\, encounter a roya
 l guard of nutcrackers\, a gingerbread house replica of the Museum\, and p
 layful elves and gnomes up to mischief\, adding a touch of whimsy for litt
 le ones. In addition to the holiday installation\, guests can enjoy the te
 mporary exhibition\, “Brave-Too-Much”: The Legend of John Coffee Hays.
  Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to fully experience the h
 oliday installation and exhibition Extended Tuesday and Thursday Tour Hour
 s: New this year\, visitors can enjoy extended hours on Tuesdays and Thurs
 days\, with last entry at 7:15 p.m. These extended guided and self-guided 
 tour hours offer greater opportunities to experience the Museum after dark
 \, when holiday décor glows with flickering candlelight and twinkling lig
 hts. Upon arrival\, visitors will discover the path and outdoor Courtyard
 \, arches and towers aglow with festive holiday lighting\, creating a trul
 y magical seasonal atmosphere. Visitors will have more time to explore the
  Museum’s holiday decorations and experience the beauty of this historic
  site after dark. Admission pricing varies\, please visit our website for 
 accurate pricing. Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to take 
 in the full holiday grandeur. Museum member benefits apply.\n\nSources: No
 rth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-
 at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-12-19/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-at-hammond-castle-museu
 m/2026-12-19/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gingerbread House Making at Wequassett
DTSTART:20261219T000000
DTEND:20261219T000000
DTSTAMP:20261119T195526Z
UID:119d2f40829995380361fcc8101921@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Gather the family for an afternoon of frosting\, sprinkles\, a
 nd holiday imagination at Wequassett. Inside the festive Waterfront Pavili
 on\, gingerbread houses become snowy cottages\, candy-covered hideaways\, 
 and whatever else your imagination dreams up. Build\, decorate\, and make 
 a little merry together as you sip steaming cups of hot cocoa and enjoy a 
 complimentary buffet created just for little ones. Festive cocktails will 
 be available for adults to purchase\, making this a holiday tradition ever
 yone can enjoy. Whether your gingerbread house is perfectly polished or wo
 nderfully whimsical\, the best part is making it together. Open to the pub
 lic\, members\, and resort guests! More Details here: Gingerbread House Pa
 rties | Wequassett\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.c
 apecodchamber.org/event/gingerbread-house-making-at-wequassett/52507/
LOCATION:Wequassett Resort & Golf Club\, 2173 Route 28\, Harwich\, MA\, 02
 645
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/gingerbread-house-making-at-wequa
 ssett/52507/
END:VEVENT
